<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n82665" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πέρσ-ης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>, ὁ, heterocl. acc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πέρσεα</span>
		v. l. in <i><span class="en">
			Hdt.
			8.108
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			109
		</span></i>; voc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πέρσᾰ</span> (but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πέρση</span> when it is the pr. n. of a person,
			Hdn.Gr.<i><span class="en">
			2.690
		</span></i>):— <u>Persian</u>, <i><span class="en">
			Hdt.
			1.4
		</span></i>, etc. (The Greeks derived the name of the people from Perseus,
			<i><span class="en">
			Id.
			7.61
		</span></i>.) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πέρσαι, οἱ</span>, the city of <u>Persepolis</u>, <i><span class="en">
				Beros.
				16
			</span></i> (leg. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">&lt;καὶ&gt;
			π.</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Arr.
				<u>An.</u>
				3.18.10
			</span></i>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Περσέπολις</span>.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> freq. as pr.n.,
				<u>Perses</u>, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Op.</u>
				10
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				27
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				7.61
			</span></i>, etc.; name of a Titan, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				409
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> the name of
				<i>a throw on the dice</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
